1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,619
Before sunrise, a shipment is ready to leave.

2
00:00:03,619 --> 00:00:07,647
For the team behind it, the job is bigger than moving freight.

3
00:00:07,647 --> 00:00:10,313
It's keeping a promise across a continent.

4
00:00:10,313 --> 00:00:12,536
Then the conditions change.

5
00:00:12,536 --> 00:00:14,091
A weather warning.

6
00:00:14,091 --> 00:00:15,855
Rising rainfall.

7
00:00:15,855 --> 00:00:17,438
A rail update.

8
00:00:17,438 --> 00:00:19,119
Separate signals.

9
00:00:19,119 --> 00:00:21,063
One decision to make.

10
00:00:21,063 --> 00:00:25,786
Atlas IQ's Corridor Lifeline concept brings those signals together.

11
00:00:25,786 --> 00:00:31,397
So the team can review the risk, rethink the shipment plan, and prepare the paperwork.

12
00:00:31,397 --> 00:00:33,661
An emergency permit draft.

13
00:00:33,661 --> 00:00:35,508
A clear risk summary.

14
00:00:35,508 --> 00:00:37,925
Ready for a person to review.

15
00:00:37,925 --> 00:00:40,466
The weather is beyond our control.

16
00:00:40,466 --> 00:00:42,897
Preparation doesn't have to be.

17
00:00:42,897 --> 00:00:44,522
Atlas IQ.

18
00:00:44,522 --> 00:00:46,563
Anticipate disruption.

19
00:00:46,563 --> 00:00:48,397
Prepare your response.

